{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789783134,"nonce":"4hWdFko1phpn4JldVmdNLeR0o0I=","title":"A loop the LLVM tier cannot resume kept its frame in the interpreter","message":"With LLVM as tier 2 the promotion requester aims at tier 2 and the Cranelift\ntier's helpers are not published. The LLVM tier makes no resume point for\na loop whose region contains a call or an allocation (nearly every Python\nloop), so the interpreted or tier-0 frame that asked for promotion never\ntransferred: a 2M-iteration loop stayed interpreted end to end (234 ms\nagainst 18 ms once transferred) even after the function was compiled at\ntier 2.\n\nFix: after a tier-2 compile, the headers left without a helper get the\nCranelift tier-1 helper, compiled without touching the call cell.","files":null}]}